WEBVTT

00:00:00.632 --> 00:00:01.966
MXI.

00:00:02.219 --> 00:00:05.308
Our team extends RoboICL with

00:00:05.308 --> 00:00:07.495
clearer geometry and checked motion.

00:00:08.518 --> 00:00:10.131
Start with one demonstration.

00:00:10.394 --> 00:00:14.242
Sample short windows to show the model how the task unfolds.

00:00:14.891 --> 00:00:18.201
Each window connects an observation, recorded actions,

00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:21.060
execution feedback, and the resulting observation.

00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:24.280
The current episode uses the same format.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.008
Completed actions become experience.

00:00:28.059 --> 00:00:30.908
Earlier time anchors and the latest segment join the

00:00:30.908 --> 00:00:33.984
demonstration and current view in the agent context.

00:00:35.284 --> 00:00:38.469
MXI keeps this feedback loop: decide, act, observe.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.596
The model weights stay frozen.

00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:44.020
Where will the fingers close?

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.601
MXI makes the grasp center explicit in the wrist image.

00:00:48.692 --> 00:00:50.431
The camera already exists.

00:00:50.684 --> 00:00:53.574
MXI adds a projected center and inner

00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:55.302
finger edges from known geometry.

00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:59.267
Watch the guide: an offset is visible, then

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.442
the tube approaches the closing center.

00:01:02.025 --> 00:01:03.262
Align, close, lift.

00:01:03.507 --> 00:01:05.224
The highlight explains alignment.

00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:07.527
Object motion shows retention.

00:01:08.506 --> 00:01:11.543
MXI target geometry locates the vase

00:01:11.543 --> 00:01:13.903
opening from recorded R G B views.

00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:17.440
Match the same opening in the head and wrist images.

00:01:17.704 --> 00:01:19.856
Each pixel defines a spatial ray.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.721
One ray leaves depth unknown.

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:26.723
Two calibrated rays recover a position, without a depth map.

00:01:27.646 --> 00:01:30.098
The reconstructed depth is half a metre.

00:01:30.362 --> 00:01:32.598
The occluded right view is excluded.

00:01:34.446 --> 00:01:36.862
The recorded lip-to-mouth offset falls from

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:40.263
seventy-eight to three millimetres before pouring.

00:01:42.504 --> 00:01:44.778
MXI checks motion before execution.

00:01:45.019 --> 00:01:48.263
A destination alone does not guarantee a reachable route.

00:01:48.896 --> 00:01:51.636
The first preview fails inverse kinematics.

00:01:51.913 --> 00:01:53.223
The robot stays still.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.036
Another plan passes.

00:01:56.312 --> 00:02:00.134
Watch the ghost hand preview recorded joint targets, step by step.

00:02:00.784 --> 00:02:04.038
These translucent poses visualize recorded commands.

00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:06.039
The numbers track the joint targets.

00:02:06.746 --> 00:02:11.262
Then the recorded arm grasps, lifts, transfers, aligns, and pours.

00:02:11.837 --> 00:02:13.105
Task score: one hundred.

00:02:13.345 --> 00:02:15.618
A later return-home warning remains logged.

00:02:16.561 --> 00:02:21.622
MXI builds on a compact RoboICL foundation: about

00:02:21.622 --> 00:02:24.076
six thousand characters in the authored-text audit.

00:02:24.775 --> 00:02:28.957
Across three exploratory task groups, our context-based system

00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:32.912
loses fewer points than Q0 when readable priors are removed.

00:02:34.402 --> 00:02:40.179
MXI RoboICL: seventy-five point nine in our self-evaluation.

00:02:40.441 --> 00:02:42.401
Geometry meets deliberate action.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.233
MXI RoboICL.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:10.759
Extended by our team.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.576
Thank you.
